    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d218">

                <pb facs="0178" n="166" xml:id="pg166"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">833.34/77: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-08-16T12:00:00-03:30">August 16,
                        1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 12:31 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>183. Your air mail despatch 119 of August 6<anchor n="40" xml:id="d218-f1"/> made
                    no mention of the Uruguayan request concerning possibility of buying destroyers
                    (see my despatch No. 398, July 1<anchor n="40" xml:id="d218-f2"/>). Please
                    telegraph what I can reply to the Uruguayan Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
